The algorithm (dense version):

```
Input: cost matrix c[i][j], i,j = 0..n-1
Output: assignment x[j] = row assigned to column j

Step 0: Initialize
  u[i] = 0 for all i
  v[j] = 0 for all j
  x[j] = -1 (unassigned) for all j
  y[i] = -1 (unassigned) for all i

Step 1: Column reduction
  for j = 0..n-1:
    find i0 = argmin_i c[i][j]
    v[j] = c[i0][j]
    if y[i0] == -1:
      y[i0] = j; x[j] = i0
    else:
      x[j] = i0; y[i0] = -2  (row i0 assigned to multiple columns)

Step 2: Reduction transfer
  for i = 0..n-1:
    if y[i] == -2:  (row i assigned to multiple columns)
